            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Foreign Policy and Military Actions</strong><br>\nPutin's foreign policy has been assertive, involving the annexation of Crimea in 2014, military intervention in Syria, and efforts to restore Russia's influence as a global power.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Domestic Policies and Public Image</strong><br>\nDomestically, Putin's government has been characterized by conservative cultural values, nationalism, and the suppression of dissent, all contributing to his maintained popularity in Russia.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Current Status and Global Impact</strong><br>\nAs of my last update, Putin remains a dominant figure in Russian politics, with changes to the constitution allowing him to potentially stay in power until 2036, shaping the nation's future and international relations.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
